{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8f3c1a52-4d21-4b9e-9c77-0a1e6b2f9d10",
    "name": "Bookstore GraphQL API",
    "description": "Full coverage of the Bookstore GraphQL schema: auth, books, and book listings.\n\n## Setup\n1. Set the `baseUrl` collection variable (default `http://localhost:8080/graphql`).\n2. Run **Signup - Author** then **Signup - Supplier** (or the two Login requests) once. Their scripts store `authorToken` / `supplierToken` and the matching user ids automatically.\n3. Book requests send `authorToken`, Listing requests send `supplierToken` (set at folder level).\n4. `createBook` stores `bookId`, `createListing` stores `listingId`, so the rest of the requests chain without manual copy-paste.\n\nThe collection can be run end-to-end with the Collection Runner in the order the requests appear.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Shared assertions applied to every request in the collection.",
          "pm.test('HTTP 200', function () {",
          "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
          "});",
          "",
          "pm.test('No GraphQL errors', function () {",
          "    var body = pm.response.json();",
          "    if (body.errors) {",
          "        console.log('GraphQL errors:', JSON.stringify(body.errors, null, 2));",
          "    }",
          "    pm.expect(body.errors, JSON.stringify(body.errors)).to.be.undefined;",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
